CODE REVIEW AND TEST RUN 2 EVALUATION
Research Papers Assistant (MIT xPro 8.1 capstone)
Files reviewed:
  Ranjan_Research_Assistant_Final_Capstone_Submission.py   (updated source, about 2,680 lines)
  Test_Research_Assistant.py                               (updated harness, 570 lines)
  research_assistant_test_case_v2_run2_results.xlsx        (158 cases, run 2 actual results)
Reference documents: research_assistant_spec.md, research_assistant_architecture.md,
  research_assistant_spec_design.md, research_assistant_test_strategy.md
Graded workbook (columns F, J, K filled): research_assistant_test_case_v2_run2_graded.xlsx


======================================================================
1. HOW THIS REVIEW WAS DONE
======================================================================

Every one of the 158 rows was read against its Expected Result and Test Result Criteria.
I did not have the model, so I could not re-run chat questions. Where the Actual Result
was enough, I graded from it. Where I could check something myself against the real
corpus text (the 153-paper text cache, 18,398,803 characters, which I loaded without the
LLM) or the submitted code, I did, and column J of the workbook says so. The checks I ran
myself were:

  - corpus statistics (153 papers, 18,398,803 characters)                      TC-072
  - BM25 retrieval for specific questions (retrieve_chunks, same k and per_doc
    as the chat path)                                                          TC-007, TC-057, TC-073, TC-078
  - quote verification on real and made-up quotes (_quote_support)             TC-027, TC-029, TC-095
  - routing and intent (route, classify_intent)                                TC-047, TC-049, TC-155 (routing half)
  - duplicate and mislabeled-document scans of the corpus                      TC-054, TC-058, year-data finding
  - benchmark scorer with a wrong answer (_eval)                               TC-117
  - make_llm with dummy settings (argument honoured, planner kept separate)    TC-106 (first half)
  - assembled hardened prompt                                                  TC-154
  - sanitizer on the benign question list, injection scan of all chunks        TC-118
  - py_compile and import of the submitted file in an empty folder             TC-129
  - dispatcher and header text read in the source                              TC-116, TC-125

Result values used: Pass, Fail, Accepted limitation, Blocked, Not Run. A manual case with
no evidence stays Not Run. A harness "PASS" was overridden where the evidence disagreed
(TC-026). Where my own run decided a row that the harness skipped, the row says so.


