7. CHANGES NEEDED IN THE TEST WORKBOOK ITSELF
======================================================================

- TC-090 and TC-108 expect "no year" for natosec_40. The submission now sets 2026 from the
  arXiv stamp ("5 May 2026"), which is correct. Change both to "title shown, year 2026". TC-024
  has the same assumption in its expected result.
- Corpus Facts and every expected result that depends on a year count (TC-025, 087, 088, 091):
  recompute after F-09 is fixed. The oracle counted 45 documents after 2020 and 15 in 2016 with
  the wrong filename years.
- TC-132 says the code reads three variables; it reads six (three optional planner variables).
  TC-126 and TC-131 say requirements.txt; the code reads requirements_8_1_v1.txt.
- TC-050: replace the 338K to 402K token baseline with the measured value for the current corpus
  (about 950K to 1.02M for the BEFORE pass), or the criterion cannot pass.
- TC-057 and TC-058 name file keys (BraggFRS21, PuNSB16) that BM25 over passage text cannot match.
  Ask the question by topic ("the CAV 2021 volume on program verification") and check the Sources
  line instead.
- TC-081: the paraphrase was answered, so the "lexical ceiling" example for the limitations slide
  has to come from TC-078 (identifier lost by the tokenizer) and TC-007.
- Accepted limitation: only TC-091 qualifies as written. TC-025 has no such clause, so it stays Fail.

Status: the corrections listed above, and the TC-055 text-yield note, are applied in research_assistant_test_case_v3.xlsx
(column N carries a "v3:" note on each changed row and the Change Log lists them).


